  "notes": [
    "Fully regular -AR verb; no spelling changes or stem changes",
    "Past participle: *tuteado*",
    "Derived from *tú* — means to use the informal *tú* form with someone rather than the formal *usted*",
    "*tutear a alguien* = to address someone as tú (*¿Puedo tutearte?* — Can I call you tú? / Can we be informal?)",
    "*tutearse* (reciprocal reflexive) = to be on first-name/informal terms with each other (*Nos tuteamos desde el primer día* — We used tú with each other from the first day)",
    "Opposite concept: *tratar de usted* = to address someone formally",
    "Related: *el tuteo* = the use of tú; *el ustedeo* = the use of usted"
  ],
